# ==============================================================================
# Order Management Platform — .gitignore
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rules for what should NEVER be committed to this repository.
#
# PRINCIPLES
#   1. Secrets before convenience. When in doubt, ignore.
#   2. Whitelist .env.example templates explicitly — the only .env* files
#      that ARE committed.
#   3. Ignore build output everywhere; never ignore build scripts or source.
#   4. Keep sections alphabetically stable within category — easier to scan.
#
# WHEN ADDING A NEW RULE
#   - Put it in the correct section.
#   - Add a one-line comment explaining WHY if the rule is non-obvious.
#   - Test with: git check-ignore -v <path>
#
# ==============================================================================

# ==============================================================================
# 1. ENVIRONMENT FILES
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any file that might contain runtime configuration or secrets.
# We ignore ALL .env* variants, then explicitly un-ignore the templates.
#
# The pattern below catches: .env, .env.local, .env.prod, .env.backup,
# .env.prod.bak, .env.2024-11-01, .env.old, .env.save, etc.
# ==============================================================================
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.prod.example

# Explicit belt-and-suspenders for the two templates (some tools treat
# `!.env.example` as a no-op when the parent directory is ignored).
!.env.*.example

# ==============================================================================
# 2. SECRET MATERIAL
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files that are definitionally secrets. Even if they appear in a subdirectory
# with an innocuous name, they should never be committed.
#
# Docker secrets are mounted from /etc/omp/secrets/ on the host, so they
# should never appear in the repo tree — but if someone dumps them here for
# debugging, this list ensures they don't get committed.
# ==============================================================================
# Private keys and certificates
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.truststore

# SSH / TLS artefacts
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*.crt.local

# Common secret directories
secrets/
.secrets/
private/
.private/
credentials/
.credentials/

# pgBackRest cipher / repo keys
*.cipher
pgbackrest.*.key

# Kafka SCRAM / SASL credential files
kafka-credentials.json
*.sasl
*.scram

# Keycloak realm exports (may contain client secrets)
# NOTE: We DO commit infrastructure/keycloak/import/*.json — those are
# hand-authored realm definitions with placeholder secrets. If you export
# a realm from a running Keycloak, that export MUST NOT be committed.
keycloak-export-*.json
*-realm-export.json

# ==============================================================================
# 3. JAVA / MAVEN BUILD OUTPUT
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Maven target directories and compiled artifacts. Never commit compiled code.
#
# IMPORTANT: Do NOT ignore the Maven wrapper (.mvn/wrapper/, mvnw, mvnw.cmd).
# The wrapper is what makes builds reproducible across machines without a
# system Maven install. It is intentionally committed.
# ==============================================================================
target/
*.class
*.jar
*.war
*.ear
*.nar

# Maven-specific
.mvn/timing.properties
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar.orig
dependency-reduced-pom.xml

# Maven build logs
build.log
mvn.log
*.mvn.log

# ==============================================================================
# 4. IDE / EDITOR
# ==============================================================================
# IntelliJ IDEA
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
out/

# Eclipse / STS
.classpath
.project
.settings/
.apt_generated/
.factorypath
.springBeans
.sts4-cache/

# Visual Studio Code
.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json

# NetBeans
nbproject/private/
nbbuild/
dist/
nbdist/
.nb-gradle/

# Vim / Neovim
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
.*.sw?
.vim/
.nvim/

# Emacs
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# Sublime
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project

# Helix
.helix/

# ==============================================================================
# 5. OS METADATA
# ==============================================================================
# macOS
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?
.fseventsd/
.Spotlight-V100/

# Windows
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# Linux
*~
.directory
.Trash-*
.nfs*

# ==============================================================================
# 6. DOCKER / LOCAL RUNTIME
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker Compose creates named volumes managed by Docker (not in the repo),
# but some tooling and debugging flows create files in the repo tree.
# ==============================================================================
# Bind-mounted data (if someone switches to bind mounts for debugging)
data/
.docker/
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.*.local.yml

# Local Docker secrets dump (if someone runs `docker secret inspect --pretty`
# and pipes to a file — should never be committed)
docker-secrets-*.txt

# Traefik ACME state if bind-mounted for debugging
acme.json

# ==============================================================================
# 7. LOGS AND COVERAGE
# ==============================================================================
*.log
logs/
*.log.gz
*.log.[0-9]*

# JaCoCo
jacoco.exec
*.exec
jacoco-report/

# Test reports (Surefire/Failsafe write to target/ which is already ignored,
# but some CI setups dump copies here)
surefire-reports/
failsafe-reports/
test-output/

# Coverage summary artefacts some tools write
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# ==============================================================================
# 8. TEMPORARY / SCRATCH
# ==============================================================================
tmp/
temp/
.tmp/
.scratch/
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.old
*.save
*.swp

# Node (future GraphQL gateway, frontend, tooling)
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.pnp.*
.yarn/cache
.yarn/install-state.gz
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Python (future tooling, scripting)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
.Python
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ==============================================================================
# 9. ARCHIVE / BACKUP FILES
# ==============================================================================
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.tar.bz2
*.rar
*.7z

# But DO commit reproducible archive producers (e.g. Makefile targets, scripts)

# ==============================================================================
# 10. METADATA FILES THAT MUST BE COMMITTED (documented here for clarity)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The following are intentionally NOT ignored. Listed here so future
# contributors don't accidentally add rules for them:
#
#   .mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar   — Maven wrapper binary (reproducible builds)
#   .mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties
#   mvnw                              — Maven wrapper script (Unix)
#   mvnw.cmd                          — Maven wrapper script (Windows)
#   .env.example                      — Dev env template (safe, no secrets)
#   .env.prod.example                 — Prod env template (safe, no secrets)
#   .vscode/settings.json             — Shared VS Code settings (un-ignored above)
#   .vscode/extensions.json           — Recommended extensions
#   .vscode/launch.json               — Shared debug configs
#   .vscode/tasks.json                — Shared build tasks
#   pom.xml                           — Maven build definition
#   Dockerfile, docker-compose*.yml   — Infrastructure definitions
#   infrastructure/**                 — All infra configs (Postgres, Keycloak, etc.)
#   docs/**                           — Documentation and runbooks
#
# If you find yourself adding an ignore rule for any of the above, STOP and
# ask why. There is almost certainly a better solution.
# ==============================================================================
# Notification client generated verification artifacts
clients/notifications/*-results.xml
clients/notifications/client-sbom.json

# Local development identities: publishing only their certificates breaks fresh setup
/infrastructure/tls/ca/
/infrastructure/tls/order-service/
/infrastructure/tls/inventory-service/
/infrastructure/tls/payment-service/

# Keep the shared editor policy reachable even when the parent is globally ignored
!/.vscode/
/.vscode/*
!/.vscode/settings.json
!/.vscode/extensions.json
!/.vscode/launch.json
!/.vscode/tasks.json
